.Dd March 31, 2025
.Dt PATH_RELATIVE_TO_B 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm path_relative_to_b ,
.Nm path_relative_to ,
.Nm path_relative_to_sa
.Nd compute a relative path between two paths
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In path.h
.Ft int
.Fn path_relative_to_b "const char *p" "size_t plen" "const char *to" "size_t tolen" "stralloc *out"
.Ft int
.Fn path_relative_to "const char *path" "const char *relative_to" "stralloc *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn path_relative_to_b
function computes a relative path from the base directory
.Fa to
(of length
.Fa tolen )
to the target path
.Fa p
(of length
.Fa plen ),
storing the result in
.Fa out .
.Pp
The
.Fn path_relative_to
function is a wrapper that accepts null-terminated strings.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 1 on success.